# 3. COMPLETE USER JOURNEY

Implement the following end-to-end workflow:

1. User signs up, logs in, or enters an explicitly supported demo mode.
2. User creates a new project and describes an application.
3. AI analyzes the prompt and identifies missing requirements.
4. AI asks only essential clarification questions.
5. AI generates a structured application specification.
6. AI creates a development plan with tasks and dependencies.
7. AI selects the appropriate technology stack and architecture.
8. AI generates the project structure, components, pages, APIs, and database schema.
9. AI initializes the development environment.
10. AI builds the application and resolves compilation errors.
11. The application appears in an interactive live preview.
12. User modifies the application through conversational instructions.
13. AI analyzes the existing project and produces targeted changes.
14. User can inspect code, diffs, logs, and generated files.
15. AI runs tests and validates the changes.
16. User saves, restores, duplicates, or exports the project.
17. User connects GitHub or configures a deployment provider.
18. AI prepares the production build and deployment configuration.
19. The application is deployed and receives a verified public URL.
20. User can continue modifying the deployed project's source through BuildMint AI.

Maintain a seamless workflow without unnecessary page reloads or loss of project state.

